bbb: an auto-increment fixup could produce an insn that fails its constraints.

opt_autoinc turns "move.l (a3),a2" into "move.l (a3)+,a2" and lowers the
offsets of the later uses of a3 (auto_inc_fixup). The fixup re-emits each of
those insns, so they are recognized anew, and recog takes the first pattern
whose predicates match. That need not be the pattern the insn had:

    lea ([11054,a3],1),a0      ; *lea: (set a0 (plus (mem (plus a3 11054)) 1))

is re-emitted with offset 11050 and recognized as *addsi3_internal, whose
constraints do not allow a memory source with an address register as
destination. Nothing checked the constraints, so the compiler crashed in final:

    error: insn does not satisfy its constraints:
    (insn 84 ... (set (reg:SI 8 a0)
            (plus:SI (mem/v:SI (plus:SI (reg/v/f:SI 11 a3) (const_int 11054))) (const_int 1))))
       {*addsi3_internal}
    internal compiler error: in final_scan_insn, at final.c:2943

Reduced from v4net.device (ApolloTeam-dev/V4Net, netdev.c, drv_dma_alloc):
a "volatile ULONG" increment at a large struct offset between Forbid() and
Permit(), -O2 with -m68020 or -m68080. -fbbb=- compiled it. Issue #33.

The fix tries each fixup on a copy of the insn first (auto_inc_fixup_valid:
patch the offsets as auto_inc_fixup does, then insn_invalid_p) and gives up the
auto increment if the result is not a valid insn, the same way try_auto_inc
already gives up on insns it cannot fix up. That spot is then compiled as with
-fbbb=-.

--- a/gcc/bbb-opts.c
+++ b/gcc/bbb-opts.c
@@ -1296,6 +1296,9 @@
 
   void
   auto_inc_fixup (int regno, int size, int addend);
+
+  bool
+  auto_inc_fixup_valid (int regno, int size, int addend);
 
   void
   patch_mem_offsets(rtx x, int size);
@@ -1505,6 +1508,33 @@
 
   SET_INSN_DELETED(insn);
   insn = emit_insn_after (pattern, insn);
+}
+
+/* True if auto_inc_fixup (REGNO, SIZE, ADDEND) yields a valid insn. The fixup re-emits the
+   insn, so it is recognized anew: recog takes the first pattern whose predicates match, which
+   need not be the one the insn had. E.g. "lea ([n,a3],1),a0" was *lea, but the re-emitted
+   (set a0 (plus (mem (plus a3 n)) 1)) becomes *addsi3_internal, whose constraints refuse it
+   (ICE "insn does not satisfy its constraints" in final). Try the fixup on a copy.  */
+bool
+insn_info::auto_inc_fixup_valid (int regno, int size, int addend)
+{
+  // add to register: only the constant shrinks, or the add is deleted
+  if (get_src_op () == PLUS && !is_src_mem() && !is_dst_mem())
+    return true;
+
+  rtx_insn * test = make_insn_raw (copy_rtx (PATTERN (insn)));
+  rtx set = single_set (test);
+  if (!set)
+    return false;
+  if (is_compare ())
+    set = SET_SRC(set);
+
+  if (get_src_mem_regno () == regno)
+    patch_mem_offsets (SET_SRC(set), get_src_mem_addr() - size * addend);
+  if (get_dst_mem_regno () == regno)
+    patch_mem_offsets (SET_DEST(set), get_dst_mem_addr() - size * addend);
+
+  return !insn_invalid_p (test, 0);
 }
 
